196 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 165 0 R
/E (Urban transportation and global logistics networks require massive investments, where inefficient route planning inevitably leads to higher operational costs and longer travel times. To address this challenge, our proposed project simulates the behavior of the slime mold Physarum polycephalum, an organism naturally adept at constructing highly efficient and resilient pathways. By deploying bio-inspired computational algorithms, the system evaluates transport hubs as discrete nodes, automatically strengthening optimal routes while pruning weaker paths. Ultimately, this nature-inspired approach aims to evaluate large-scale Indian transit corridors and supply chains, providing planners with reliable, sustainable methods to design smarter, future-ready networks. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
